  "result": "My implementation is in place and builds, but all 4 target tests still fail, and the cause is outside my file.\n\nThe setter is correct, but `Iterator.prototype.constructor` is overwritten after installation. The link loop in `crates/kahvi-builtins/src/table.rs:899-903` runs for every constructor, including `%Iterator%`, and defines `constructor` on the prototype as a plain data property. That replaces the accessor pair from `generated.rs`, so `desc.get` and `desc.set` are both undefined. Fixing this needs a change to `table.rs`, which is outside my scope. The same problem will likely affect the sibling `Symbol.toStringTag` accessor, but I have not checked that.\n\nWhat I did in `prototype_set_constructor.rs`:\n- Implemented the steps with spec comments. Step 1 calls a private helper `setter_that_ignores_prototype_properties`, and step 2 returns `undefined`.\n- I put the `SetterThatIgnoresPrototypeProperties` helper in this file because it does not exist anywhere in the engine yet. `prototype_set_symbol_to_string_tag.rs` needs the same helper, so it should move to `support/` once that ticket runs.\n- `cargo build` and `cargo clippy` are clean for this file, and rustfmt has run.\n\nBLOCKED: `table.rs` link loop (lines ~899-903) overwrites the `Iterator.prototype.constructor` accessor with a data property; it must skip that accessor or the helper must move into `support/`.",
